# SAFETY GUARDRAIL — this repo is PUBLIC (GitHub Pages).
# Default to ignoring EVERYTHING, then explicitly allow only the
# files that are meant to be public (the website + the trivia apps).
# This makes it impossible for a stray `git add -A` to push sensitive
# business files (Financials, Customer Contracts, client lists, memory,
# notes, etc.) to the public repo. Those files stay on disk, untouched —
# they're just invisible to git.

# Ignore all top-level entries by default
/*

# ...but allow the public website, the trivia apps, and this file
!/.gitignore
!/docs/
!/Trivia/
